WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.040
Is repulsion a fixed property of Sema3A?

2
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.640
Or can the growth cone change the answer?

3
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:13.640
Song, Poo and colleagues grew single frog spinal neurons in a dish.

4
00:00:14.633 --> 00:00:19.553
A fine pipette set up a small gradient of Sema3A beside one growth cone.

5
00:00:20.433 --> 00:00:21.653
The growth cone turned away.

6
00:00:22.633 --> 00:00:25.993
Now raise cyclic GMP inside the growth cone.

7
00:00:26.933 --> 00:00:28.153
Same pipette, same gradient.

8
00:00:29.193 --> 00:00:30.193
What happens?

9
00:00:35.817 --> 00:00:38.177
The growth cone turned toward the Sema3A.

10
00:00:38.937 --> 00:00:40.217
The gradient did not change.

11
00:00:41.177 --> 00:00:42.177
The reader did.

12
00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:49.380
Cyclic GMP is a second messenger made by guanylate cyclases.

13
00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:52.540
Here, its level sets the sign of the answer.

14
00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:57.190
A similar switch, with cyclic AMP, governs netrin.

15
00:00:58.183 --> 00:01:00.063
Does a living neuron use this switch?

16
00:01:01.043 --> 00:01:02.363
Look at the developing cortex.

17
00:01:03.417 --> 00:01:07.917
Sema3A is high near the pial surface, the outer surface of the brain.

18
00:01:08.777 --> 00:01:11.597
It repels the axons of cortical neurons downward.

19
00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:16.110
But the apical dendrite of the same neuron grows up, toward it.

20
00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:18.033
Why the difference?

21
00:01:19.153 --> 00:01:24.533
Soluble guanylate cyclase, an enzyme that makes cyclic GMP, sits mainly in the

22
00:01:24.533 --> 00:01:25.533
developing dendrite.

23
00:01:26.293 --> 00:01:27.713
It is needed for that attraction.

24
00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:32.727
One cue, one neuron, two answers, set by where the enzyme is.

25
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:34.950
Now replay the rule.

26
00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:36.910
The cue marks the place.

27
00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.490
The growth cone decides what it means.

28
00:01:40.483 --> 00:01:44.983
The pain fibre and the muscle afferent differ in how strongly they answer the cue.

29
00:01:46.017 --> 00:01:49.277
The axon and the dendrite differ in which way they answer.

30
00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:54.207
For a repelled growth cone, a pipette gradient typically gives a turn.

31
00:01:55.087 --> 00:01:59.187
A strong dose in a bath can give a collapse, where the preparation supports it.

32
00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:03.760
The takeaway: semaphorins keep axons out of wrong places.

33
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:08.540
But only axons that can hear them, and only in the sense their state allows.
